# A case builds the `team-launcher` parser (or runs `main` to its own `--help`) and parses a synthetic argv; nothing is
# dispatched. The program name and the help width are pinned (argv[0] `team-launcher`, COLUMNS=100) so the output is
# the parser's, not the terminal's. Recorded: the parsed namespace, or argparse's exit code, and exactly what it
# printed to stdout and stderr. Paths under the launcher's checkout read REPO. Names the parser reads through the
# launcher are rebound there by their own cases; the pane-state default, which the environment decides at import, is
# pinned there in every case.
